  "observations": "Short-pad chromatography\nFritted funnel (50mL, por. 4), suction adapter, 100 mL RBF, T-connector, diaphragm pump\nAdd 15 g of neutral alumina\nAdd THF to fully wet the alumina\nAdd the reaction mixture\nElute with suction and THF until the eluate becomes pale red → 70 mL, alumina pad (Green at the top, off white at the bottom)\nRotovap\nDry under vacuum Schlenk line, 1 h \nDark brown solid\n\nRT 21.9 °C, RH 32 %\nCHCl₃ deacidification\n250 mL RBF\nAdd basic alumina 20 g\nAdd CHCl₃ 150 mL and swirl\nFritted funnel (50 mL, por. 4), suction adapter, 250 mL RBF, diaphragm pump\nFilter the mixture under suction\n\nReprecipitation\nAdd 30 mL of purified CHCl₃ to the flask and sonicate → dark red solution\nAdd 180 mL of n-hexane, swirl, sonicate\nStore in fridge (0 °C) for 1 h\nFritted funnel (50 mL, por. 4), suction adapter, 500 mL RBF, diaphragm pump \nFilter the mixture under suction → faint brown filtrate\nRinse w/ 2 x (10 mL of purified CHCl₃ + 60 mL of hexane)\nRinse with 2 × 30 mL of petroleum ether [hexane should be used]\nDry under vacuum (desiccator, diaphragm pump, overnight) → reddish brown solid\n\nAnalysis\nRT 20.4 °C, RH 45%\n20 mL vial with PTFE sealing (tare: 15.52848 g)\nWeigh : 575.90 g\n→ 1H NMR P (CDCl₃; U1.834; N PROTON 20 ppm; O1P 6, SW 22) (dark red solution)  [should be measured in DMSO as well]\nStore in the fridge",
